  "explanation": "Sparse GO-only feature (nonzero on 1.3% of steps, max ~0.7; it is exactly 0 at D1 and D2). Its magnitude is large (0.2-0.55) at GO after a rewarded visit to S1, mainly after a1 S1 r (common rewarded). It is bigger when the trial before was also a1 S1 r (a streak), and when the a1 policy logit margin (choice) is moderate (about 1-7, peaking at 1-3). It is about 0 when the policy is saturated (choice > 7). It also depends strongly on episode position, beyond the phase x decile baseline: it ramps up from trial ~30 to a peak at trials 70-79, then drops sharply after trial 80. After a2 S1 r (rare rewarded) it is weaker. It is ~0 after any S2 outcome or an unrewarded trial. A term for the window first trial (previous trial unknown, rewarded, choice in 0-7) captures the windows that open mid-streak. Hidden good state and since_rev add only ~0.005 on dev. Test R^2 beyond timing 0.446 (dev 0.487) with 5 terms, which is well above the additive all ceiling of 0.15 because the terms are interactions. Uses the model policy output (choice), but no future variables. Remaining error is mostly in rare windows that open on a long streak.",
